# =====================================================================
# Release V078 -- Recall model rebuild (two-source metrics)
# =====================================================================
# Root cause (verified): recall RECORDS are a HISTORY of cycles (Completed/Missed/Unbooked/
# Booked), materialised only ~1 month before due; Gold re-derived status from the due date,
# so completed/historical cycles were counted as "overdue" -> Overdue Recalls (3,126) and
# Retention Outlook (52%) were both wrong. The FORWARD schedule lives on the PATIENT
# (Dim_Patients.Dentist_Recall_Date / Hygienist_Recall_Date).
#
# Replaces retention_outlook + overdue_recalls with FOUR metrics:
#   dentist_retention_outlook / hygiene_retention_outlook  (FORWARD: patient recall date <=4wk,
#       numerator = future exam / scale&polish booked)               -> ~77.7% / ~79.6%
#   dentist_recall_conversion / hygiene_recall_conversion  (REACTIVE: recall records where a
#       reminder was sent + concluded, real Status Completed vs Missed) -> ~95.6% / ~95.3%
#
#   * usp_Load_Fact_Metric_Actuals: new #ret (Dim_Patients) + #conv (Fact_Recalls.Status) blocks.
#   * Config.Metric_Definitions: 4 new rows; retention_outlook + overdue_recalls set Is_Active=0.
#
# C# (NOT a warehouse deploy): TabularEditor_Patients.csx + TabularEditor_MetricActuals.csx --
# re-apply in Tabular Editor + refresh the model.
#
# Run: .\Scripts\Deploy.ps1 -Manifest Releases\V078__recall_two_source_metrics.manifest -SkipTests
# =====================================================================

DEPLOY  Fabric\Gold.usp_Load_Fact_Metric_Actuals.StoredProcedure.sql
DEPLOY  Fabric\Config.Metric_Definitions.Data.sql

TEST
